# Cursor Rules for Care Progression Project

## TailwindCSS Styling Rules

### MANDATORY: Use TailwindCSS for all styling
- Always use TailwindCSS utility classes instead of custom CSS
- Never write inline styles or custom CSS classes
- Use existing TailwindCSS configuration from ui/tailwind.config.js

### Class Organization
- Order classes: layout → spacing → typography → colors → effects
- Example: `flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow`

### Color Usage Guidelines
- **Semantic colors available**: `clblue`, `clgrey`, `clpurple` for brand consistency
- **Generic colors allowed**: Standard TailwindCSS colors like `blue-500`, `gray-300`, etc.
- **Recommended approach**: Use semantic colors for brand elements, generic colors for general UI
- **Status colors**: `green` (success), `red` (error), `yellow` (warning), `blue` (info)

**Color Examples:**
```jsx
// Preferred for brand elements (navigation, headers, primary buttons)
<button className="bg-clblue hover:bg-clblue-dark text-white">
<h1 className="text-clblue font-bold">

// Acceptable for general UI (cards, borders, secondary elements)
<div className="border border-gray-300 bg-gray-50">
<button className="bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-600 text-white">

// Status colors for feedback
<div className="bg-green-100 border border-green-300 text-green-700">
<div className="bg-red-100 border border-red-300 text-red-700">

// Both approaches are valid - choose based on context
<div className="text-clgrey-dark">Brand-aligned text</div>
<div className="text-gray-600">General UI text</div>
```

### Component Standards
- Buttons: `px-4 py-2` for standard buttons
- Cards: `shadow-md` for standard cards, `hover:shadow-lg` for interactive cards
- Form inputs: `rounded-lg` border radius
- Icons: `w-5 h-5` for inline icons, `w-6 h-6` for larger icons

### Responsive Design
- Mobile-first approach: base styles for mobile, then responsive variants
- Use breakpoints: `sm:` (600px), `md:` (960px), `lg:` (1280px), `xl:` (1920px)

## Internationalization (i18n) Rules

### MANDATORY: All text must use i18n keys
- NEVER hardcode text strings in components
- ALWAYS use `useTranslation('app')` hook for text
- Use `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` for i18n keys

### Required i18n Implementation
```javascript
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';

const MyComponent = () => {
  const { t } = useTranslation('app');
  
  return (
    <button className="px-4 py-2 bg-clblue text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-clblue-dark">
      {t('SAVE_BUTTON_LABEL')}
    </button>
  );
};
```

### i18n Namespaces
- Use `'app'` for general UI text
- Use `'pages'` for page-specific content
- Use `'adminApp'` for admin features

### Common i18n Keys Available
- Buttons: `SAVE_BUTTON_LABEL`, `CANCEL_BUTTON_LABEL`, `DELETE_BUTTON_LABEL`, `EDIT_BUTTON_LABEL`
- Status: `ACTIVE_STATUS`, `INACTIVE_STATUS`, `PENDING_STATUS`, `COMPLETED_STATUS`
- Messages: `LOADING_MESSAGE`, `NO_DATA_AVAILABLE`, `SAVE_SUCCESS_MESSAGE`
- Validation: `REQUIRED_FIELD_ERROR`, `INVALID_EMAIL_ERROR`

## Material-UI Integration Rules

### Combining MUI with TailwindCSS
- Use TailwindCSS classes in `className` prop for MUI components
- Maintain consistency with existing theme
- Example: `<Button className="bg-clblue hover:bg-clblue-dark">`

## Code Generation Requirements

### Component Structure Template
```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';
import { /* MUI components */ } from '@mui/material';

const ComponentName = ({ props }) => {
  const { t } = useTranslation('app');

  return (
    <div className="p-4 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md">
      <h2 className="text-xl font-semibold text-clblue mb-4">
        {t('COMPONENT_TITLE')}
      </h2>
      {/* Component content with TailwindCSS classes and i18n */}
    </div>
  );
};

export default ComponentName;
```

### MANDATORY Checklist for Generated Code
- [ ] All text uses i18n keys with `useTranslation` hook
- [ ] TailwindCSS classes are ordered correctly
- [ ] Colors are chosen appropriately (semantic for brand, generic for general UI)
- [ ] Responsive design is implemented
- [ ] Component follows existing patterns
- [ ] No hardcoded text strings
- [ ] No custom CSS classes

### Form Components Rules
```javascript
// Always structure forms like this:
<form className="space-y-4">
  <div className="flex flex-col">
    <label className="text-sm font-medium text-clgrey-dark mb-1">
      {t('NAME_LABEL')}
    </label>
    <input 
      className="px-3 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:ring-2 focus:ring-clblue focus:border-transparent"
      placeholder={t('SEARCH_PLACEHOLDER')}
    />
  </div>
</form>
```

### Table Components Rules
```javascript
// Use consistent table styling:
<div className="overflow-x-auto">
  <table className="min-w-full bg-white shadow-md rounded-lg">
    <thead className="bg-clgrey-light">
      <tr>
        <th className="px-6 py-3 text-left text-xs font-medium text-clgrey-dark uppercase tracking-wider">
          {t('NAME_LABEL')}
        </th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
  </table>
</div>
```

### Error Handling Template
```javascript
// Always include error states with i18n:
{error && (
  <div className="p-4 bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-lg">
    <p className="text-red-700 text-sm">
      {t('NETWORK_ERROR_MESSAGE')}
    </p>
  </div>
)}

{loading && (
  <div className="flex items-center justify-center p-8">
    <p className="text-clgrey-dark">{t('LOADING_MESSAGE')}</p>
  </div>
)}
```

## JavaScript/React ESLint Rules

### MANDATORY: Follow ESLint Configuration
- All JavaScript/React code must follow the project's ESLint configuration
- Based on Airbnb style guide with Prettier integration
- Use React 17+ patterns (no React imports needed for JSX)

### Code Formatting Standards

#### **Import Organization**
```javascript
// 1. React and core libraries first
import React, { useState, useEffect, useCallback, useMemo } from 'react';

// 2. Third-party libraries
import { Button, Typography, Box } from '@mui/material';
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';
import { useDispatch, useSelector } from 'react-redux';

// 3. Internal imports (services, utils, components)
import FuseLoading from '@fuse/core/FuseLoading';
import { fetchData, clearData } from '../../store/slices/dataSlice';
import { selectUser } from '../../store/userSlice';

// 4. Remove unused imports automatically
```

#### **Function Declarations**
```javascript
// Prefer arrow functions for components
const MyComponent = ({ prop1, prop2, prop3 }) => {
  // Component logic
};

// Multi-line parameters
const MyComponent = ({
  prop1,
  prop2,
  prop3,
  onAction,
  defaultValues = {},
}) => {
  // Component logic
};

// Callbacks with proper formatting
const handleAction = useCallback(
  (param) => {
    // Action logic
  },
  [dependency1, dependency2]
);
```

#### **Object and Array Formatting**
```javascript
// Multi-line objects
const config = {
  property1: 'value1',
  property2: 'value2',
  property3: {
    nestedProp: 'value',
  },
};

// Multi-line arrays
const dependencies = [
  'dependency1',
  'dependency2',
  'dependency3',
];

// useMemo with proper formatting
const memoizedValue = useMemo(
  () => {
    return expensiveCalculation(data);
  },
  [data, otherDependency]
);
```

#### **Conditional Rendering**
```javascript
// Short conditions
{loading && <FuseLoading />}

// Multi-line conditions
{error && (
  <Typography color="error">
    {t('ERROR_MESSAGE')}
  </Typography>
)}

// Complex conditions
{data && data.length > 0 ? (
  <DataDisplay data={data} />
) : (
  <EmptyState message={t('NO_DATA_MESSAGE')} />
)}
```

#### **JSX Formatting**
```javascript
// Self-closing tags
<DialogActions />

// Multi-line JSX with proper indentation
<Button
  variant="outlined"
  onClick={handleClick}
  className="px-4 py-2 text-blue-500"
>
  {t('BUTTON_LABEL')}
</Button>

// Conditional className
<CheckIcon
  className={`w-4 h-4 ${
    isSelected ? 'text-green-600' : 'text-gray-500'
  } transition-colors`}
/>
```

#### **State and Hooks**
```javascript
// useState with proper destructuring
const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
const [data, setData] = useState([]);

// useSelector with arrow function
const user = useSelector((state) => state.user.data);
const isLoading = useSelector((state) => state.ui.loading);

// setState with function when needed
setData((prevData) => [...prevData, newItem]);
```

### ESLint Rules Enforcement

#### **Required Patterns**
- No unused variables or imports (unused-imports plugin)
- Consistent arrow function usage
- Proper trailing commas in multi-line structures
- Semi-colons at statement ends
- Single quotes for strings
- 2-space indentation
- Line length max 100 characters

#### **React-Specific Rules**
- No prop-types required (using TypeScript patterns)
- No React import needed for JSX (React 17+)
- Allow array index as key (when appropriate)
- Allow JSX props spreading
- No destructuring assignment requirement

#### **Disabled Strict Rules**
- console.log allowed for debugging
- Underscore dangle allowed
- Param reassign allowed (for Redux Toolkit)
- Global require allowed
- No use before define restriction

### Prettier Integration
```javascript
// Auto-formatting settings:
// - printWidth: 100
// - tabWidth: 2
// - singleQuote: true
// - trailingComma: 'es5'
// - arrowParens: 'always'
// - bracketSpacing: true
// - semi: true
```

### MANDATORY Code Generation Checklist
- [ ] All imports properly organized and unused ones removed
- [ ] Arrow functions used consistently
- [ ] Multi-line objects/arrays properly formatted
- [ ] JSX properly indented and formatted
- [ ] useCallback/useMemo dependencies array properly formatted
- [ ] Consistent spacing and line breaks
- [ ] Single quotes for strings, no semicolon omission
- [ ] Self-closing JSX tags where appropriate

## STRICT ENFORCEMENT
- Code generation MUST follow these ESLint rules without exception
- All JavaScript/React code should pass ESLint validation
- Prettier formatting should be applied automatically
- When in doubt, reference existing components in the codebase for patterns
- Always use appropriate i18n keys and choose colors that maintain design consistency 